# Vulnerabilities the container scan (.github/workflows/container.yml) is
# allowed to ignore. Only CRITICAL findings fail CI, so an entry here is an
# accepted, reviewed risk, not a way to silence noise.
#
# Every entry must:
#   - have a comment above it naming the affected package, why the finding
#     does not apply or cannot be fixed yet, and a link to the advisory or
#     upstream issue;
#   - carry an expiry date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD), at most 90 days out, after which
#     Trivy reports the finding again and it has to be re-reviewed.
#
# Example:
#   # openssl (alpine): only reachable through the TLS server API, which the
#   # service does not use. https://example.com/advisory
#   CVE-0000-00000 exp:2026-12-31
#
# See docs/container-image.md#vulnerability-scan.
